The use of a weighted average as the combination function allows us to account for the proportion of tiles allocated to each expert, such that the models with a larger number of tiles analysed will have a proportionally larger weight in the final prediction, while still incorporating information from all experts. See Tables 1 and 2 for the algorithm descriptions of the MoE strategy.
